    "evidence": "Expense claim EC-0419 states its claim period as 1-15 October 2026, and its receipt dates are printed DD/MM/YYYY. Six receipts fall inside that period: R1 02/10/2026 (2 Oct), R2 03/10/2026 (3 Oct), R3 06/10/2026 (6 Oct), R4 09/10/2026 (9 Oct), R5 11/10/2026 (11 Oct), R6 14/10/2026 (14 Oct). R7 is dated 17/10/2026, i.e. 17 October 2026, which is two days after the period closes, so not every receipt is dated within the claim period. The DD/MM reading is forced, not chosen: the document states the format explicitly, and a MM/DD reading of 17/10/2026 would make the month 17, which is impossible. R7 is part of the claim rather than an excluded attachment, since its 21.30 is included in the 375.14 total claimed (the seven receipts sum to exactly 375.14). The rest of the claim's arithmetic is sound - the date defect is the only one. Uncertainty: the receipt scans themselves are not reproduced, so the dates are taken as printed in this schedule.",
